WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.135 --> 00:00:02.048
- [Voiceover] Why do you like pie so much?

00:00:02.048 --> 00:00:03.882
- Okay this is why I like pie so much:

00:00:03.882 --> 00:00:05.510
pastry dough, filling,

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:07.623
hot, flakey,

00:00:07.954 --> 00:00:08.651
crusty.

00:00:08.651 --> 00:00:10.503
(groovy music)

00:00:12.598 --> 00:00:14.339
- [Voiceover] We're in China,

00:00:14.339 --> 00:00:15.511
town.

00:00:16.578 --> 00:00:18.575
About to eat some pie,
because I'm gonna eat pies

00:00:18.575 --> 00:00:19.661
from around the world.

00:00:19.922 --> 00:00:21.640
Reppin' China, where I'm from,

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:22.888
Beijing Pie House.

00:00:23.009 --> 00:00:24.937
The word pie is in the title,

00:00:24.937 --> 00:00:26.734
that means that there's gonna be pie here.

00:00:26.734 --> 00:00:28.099
(groovy music)

00:00:32.649 --> 00:00:33.070
Pies.

00:00:34.304 --> 00:00:35.727
I don't think this is
gonna be like an American

00:00:35.727 --> 00:00:37.185
knife and fork pie.

00:00:38.119 --> 00:00:39.089
Obviously.

00:00:39.601 --> 00:00:41.460
So, we'll just see what we get.

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:43.072
Pie time.

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:45.040
hashtag...

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.177
wold of pie.

00:00:47.957 --> 00:00:48.808
These look like

00:00:49.208 --> 00:00:51.128
flattened giant dumpings.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:54.217
Like this, seems weird.

00:00:55.244 --> 00:00:56.734
I feel like, okay, well

00:00:56.734 --> 00:00:58.214
don't know how to do this.

00:00:58.684 --> 00:00:59.530
Eat it with my hands.

00:00:59.907 --> 00:01:00.923
Here we go.

00:01:02.243 --> 00:01:03.492
This is gonna get hot.

00:01:03.846 --> 00:01:05.558
Hot, hot, hot pocket.

00:01:05.912 --> 00:01:06.872
That's delicious.

00:01:07.783 --> 00:01:10.030
It's delicious, that does not
need any soy sauce at all.

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:11.730
That is...

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:12.409
very tasty.

00:01:12.409 --> 00:01:14.290
Pie dough should be flakey,

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:15.654
let me tell you if it has that.

00:01:17.448 --> 00:01:18.353
This is not flakey.

00:01:18.427 --> 00:01:19.447
- [Voiceover] Is it pie?

00:01:20.242 --> 00:01:21.792
- (chuckles) I don't know if this is pie.

00:01:22.806 --> 00:01:24.566
I don't know if this is pie.

00:01:24.919 --> 00:01:26.129
Verdict is: delicious,

00:01:26.335 --> 00:01:28.419
confused as to whether
or not it's still pie.

00:01:31.071 --> 00:01:33.664
Hey I just got some spinach pie,

00:01:34.846 --> 00:01:35.886
and I'm gonna eat it the way

00:01:35.886 --> 00:01:38.249
everyone should eat
spinach pie in the car.

00:01:38.908 --> 00:01:39.698
What?

00:01:40.988 --> 00:01:41.936
- Woah!

00:01:43.427 --> 00:01:44.379
Now,

00:01:44.379 --> 00:01:45.729
this is a lot of spinach pie.

00:01:45.729 --> 00:01:47.168
Here we go.

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:49.681
I notice that that's my

00:01:49.681 --> 00:01:51.097
term whenever I eat food now

00:01:51.097 --> 00:01:52.455
I go: here we go.

00:01:53.038 --> 00:01:54.616
- [Voiceover] Do you always, uh,--

00:01:54.616 --> 00:01:55.003
- I never--

00:01:55.003 --> 00:01:56.070
- [Voiceover] talk with
your mouth full too?

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:56.497
- No.

00:01:57.467 --> 00:01:58.562
Well this is delicious.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:01.125
Let's open our minds more.

00:02:01.125 --> 00:02:02.399
Does pie have to be...

00:02:03.054 --> 00:02:03.797
flakey?

00:02:03.797 --> 00:02:05.742
No, that's what we learned from China.

00:02:05.863 --> 00:02:07.731
Does pie have to be...

00:02:09.503 --> 00:02:11.730
circular? Spherical?

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:12.586
Noo.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:14.355
- [Voiceover] Well
spherical would be weird

00:02:14.355 --> 00:02:15.986
that would be like a basketball of pie.

00:02:15.986 --> 00:02:17.349
- You're right. Wrong word--

00:02:17.349 --> 00:02:18.372
- [Voiceover] That'd be delicious though.

00:02:18.372 --> 00:02:19.504
- 3-D pie.

00:02:20.009 --> 00:02:20.975
Verdict is...

00:02:21.485 --> 00:02:22.646
it's pie.

00:02:23.093 --> 00:02:24.457
(groovy music)

00:02:25.276 --> 00:02:26.547
Verdict is good.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.312
I like Greek pie.

00:02:28.596 --> 00:02:30.657
(groovy music)

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:36.165
Well I don't have to
introduce what this is

00:02:36.165 --> 00:02:38.273
because I think everyone
is familiar with quiche.

00:02:38.859 --> 00:02:40.948
I consider this a pie because

00:02:40.948 --> 00:02:41.876
it has the crust,

00:02:41.876 --> 00:02:45.098
this one has zucchini
and red pepper and feta.

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:47.675
Google translate...

00:02:48.656 --> 00:02:50.020
quiche means quiche.

00:02:50.281 --> 00:02:51.280
That's a joke from

00:02:51.794 --> 00:02:53.396
National Lampoon's European Vacation

00:02:53.396 --> 00:02:55.302
why did I fall for that? (chuckles)

00:02:55.678 --> 00:02:57.670
That is like, I knew that.

00:02:57.815 --> 00:02:59.798
I knew that already that
quiche means quiche.

00:02:59.942 --> 00:03:01.173
This is good.

00:03:03.036 --> 00:03:05.265
Let's see if the crust is
as tasty as the filling.

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:07.277
Mmhmm. Buttery.

00:03:08.511 --> 00:03:09.324
Flakey.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:10.922
You know those little

00:03:10.922 --> 00:03:12.362
noodles you get

00:03:12.362 --> 00:03:14.376
those extra noodles you
get with Chinese takeout?

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:16.675
Kinda taste like that a little bit.

00:03:17.054 --> 00:03:18.600
This is the tastiest so far.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.398
But I think we're gonna
have to stop for today.

00:03:20.728 --> 00:03:22.255
So I can finish this entire pie.

00:03:22.771 --> 00:03:23.584
And then we'll

00:03:23.584 --> 00:03:24.707
come back and do three more.

00:03:24.707 --> 00:03:25.890
(groovy music)

00:03:26.662 --> 00:03:28.519
As you can tell it's day two,

00:03:28.644 --> 00:03:29.549
because I'm wearing different clothes.

00:03:29.549 --> 00:03:30.635
We're gonna get more pie.

00:03:30.664 --> 00:03:32.774
(groovy music)

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:38.153
Day two, world of pie.

00:03:38.153 --> 00:03:40.180
This is a chicken pot pie from Australia.

00:03:40.394 --> 00:03:41.341
Mmmm.

00:03:42.159 --> 00:03:43.547
I know it's savory inside.

00:03:43.859 --> 00:03:45.856
Well I know cause I ordered it but,

00:03:45.856 --> 00:03:49.439
I can taste savoriness
waiting for me inside.

00:03:49.816 --> 00:03:51.193
Hi, can you see what's inside?

00:03:51.193 --> 00:03:52.550
Oo, you see chicken.

00:03:53.063 --> 00:03:54.544
You see vegetables.

00:03:55.362 --> 00:03:56.541
You see potatoes.

00:03:56.848 --> 00:03:58.081
This is an entire meal...

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:00.569
that's in a pie form...

00:04:01.178 --> 00:04:03.518
that's sort of like a muffin, too.

00:04:05.381 --> 00:04:07.124
I'm having a little bit of trouble here.

00:04:07.524 --> 00:04:08.577
Verdict is: very good.

00:04:08.577 --> 00:04:10.155
I would love to eat this for dinner.

00:04:10.897 --> 00:04:11.690
I think it's a good sign

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:12.936
when your hands look like this afterwards,

00:04:12.936 --> 00:04:14.736
when they're filled with buttery crumbs.

00:04:14.736 --> 00:04:16.408
- [Voiceover] And you
have a crumb on your face.

00:04:17.118 --> 00:04:18.189
- I think that's a good sign too.

00:04:18.729 --> 00:04:20.045
So now we're at Stella Barra,

00:04:20.045 --> 00:04:21.247
which is in Hollywood.

00:04:21.555 --> 00:04:23.010
And we're gonna get a pizza pie

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:24.587
to represent Italy.

00:04:24.615 --> 00:04:25.678
(groovy music)

00:04:26.287 --> 00:04:27.489
Is that roasted garlic?

00:04:27.489 --> 00:04:29.213
- Yea, this is roasted garlic, and uh,

00:04:29.213 --> 00:04:30.484
Calabrian chile.

00:04:31.535 --> 00:04:32.695
- [Voiceover] How many minutes?

00:04:32.695 --> 00:04:36.196
- Uh, right now, probably
about 10 to 12 minutes.

00:04:36.196 --> 00:04:37.328
- [Voiceover] Okay.

00:04:37.328 --> 00:04:39.004
I'll see you in 10 to 12 minutes, friend.

00:04:39.144 --> 00:04:39.915
- (laughs)

00:04:39.915 --> 00:04:40.496
- Thank you.

00:04:40.496 --> 00:04:41.401
- Yeah.

00:04:42.076 --> 00:04:43.480
- [Voiceover] I'm so excited for pizza.

00:04:44.298 --> 00:04:45.244
Pizza pie.

00:04:47.773 --> 00:04:48.844
Hi pizza.

00:04:48.849 --> 00:04:51.540
Hullo, we knew you when
you were just dough.

00:04:51.967 --> 00:04:53.059
Mmmm.

00:04:53.552 --> 00:04:54.652
Is this pie?

00:04:57.183 --> 00:04:58.118
I don't care.

00:04:58.766 --> 00:04:59.864
I honestly don't.

00:04:59.864 --> 00:05:01.696
You know what I've noticed
about all of these pies?

00:05:01.864 --> 00:05:03.275
Is that, they all have crust.

00:05:03.275 --> 00:05:04.695
Maybe that's what defines a pie,

00:05:04.695 --> 00:05:06.284
that it has to have crust;

00:05:06.284 --> 00:05:07.246
dough...

00:05:07.246 --> 00:05:09.145
surrounding a filling.

00:05:09.801 --> 00:05:10.758
I'm gonna crack that code.

00:05:10.758 --> 00:05:12.030
(groovy music)

00:05:12.755 --> 00:05:14.195
This is downtown L.A.

00:05:14.195 --> 00:05:15.582
We're about to go to The Pie Hole

00:05:15.582 --> 00:05:17.235
for the American pie.

00:05:17.444 --> 00:05:19.554
(groovy music)

00:05:27.411 --> 00:05:28.986
I'm just checking my hair.

00:05:28.986 --> 00:05:30.467
Hair looks good.

00:05:31.982 --> 00:05:33.767
It's the final stop,
we're in downtown L.A.

00:05:33.767 --> 00:05:35.131
and we're at The Pie Hole.

00:05:35.392 --> 00:05:37.732
And, I ordered an apple pie.

00:05:38.016 --> 00:05:39.532
I like that the apples are...

00:05:40.048 --> 00:05:41.737
really sweet, but very tart.

00:05:41.998 --> 00:05:43.577
It's a little crips, but not mushy

00:05:43.577 --> 00:05:44.570
at all.

00:05:46.061 --> 00:05:47.268
That's a nice crust.

00:05:47.645 --> 00:05:49.396
That is a flakey, buttery crust.

00:05:50.145 --> 00:05:51.222
This is a pie.

00:05:52.179 --> 00:05:53.358
This is definitely a pie.

00:05:53.642 --> 00:05:54.826
Get some of the cinnamon action

00:05:55.373 --> 00:05:56.523
oozing out on the side.

00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:00.354
So my verdict is that America wins,

00:06:00.354 --> 00:06:01.755
because if there's one thing

00:06:01.755 --> 00:06:02.796
that our country knows how to do,

00:06:02.796 --> 00:06:04.776
it's how to inject sugar into food.

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:06.765
And we have won

00:06:06.765 --> 00:06:08.780
big-time in the pie category.

00:06:09.110 --> 00:06:10.520
It's as American as...

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.145
this pie.

00:06:12.267 --> 00:06:15.001
(groovy music)

00:06:18.629 --> 00:06:19.999
(whooshing)

00:06:19.999 --> 00:06:21.276
(moves into creaking hinges)

